  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional Capacity Building</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A total of 120 priest and religious leaders will be invited to a one day non residential workshop which will be held once a month in the first three months. The priests and the religious will be invited through the Bishops office to ensure a high turn up and will be trained by the professionals in the legal field.   Training will be done by qualified coordinators once in every three months during their Diocesan meeting and it will cover most relevant legal topics.  Trainees will be expected to give feedback to the programme co- coordinators once in every three months during their Diocesan meeting. 

The trained paralegals and the priest will identify fifteen (15) members of the community from every parish, to include invitations to other religions as well as CBOs, who will be clustered into four regions for the residential workshops. The residential seminars will be in three phases during which the paralegal training manual will be employed.  The seminars have been planned to take place during school holidays to utilise locally available schools as residential places.  The paralegals who were trained in the past programme will be the trainers in the residential seminars.</narrative>
  </description>
